    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d801">

                <pb facs="0890" n="696" xml:id="pg696"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Hungary)/7–1845:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 801<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Representative in Hungary</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Schoenfeld</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of State</hi><anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d801-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Budapest</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-18T12:00:00+02:00">July 18, 1945—12 p.m.</date> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">sic</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>304. Mytel 291, July 16.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d801-f2"/></p>
                <p>Key has telegraphed War Department reporting substance of discussion at
                    last night’s meeting of ACC which indicates that
                    new procedure more satisfactory to US is actually contemplated and has begun
                    without formal agreement. Key did not
                    press for formalization of new procedure.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>Sent to Dept, repeated to USPolAd Frankfort as 8 and to Moscow as 30.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Schoenfeld</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d801-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d801-f1-content">
                <p>The same message was sent directly to the Office of the Political Adviser at
                    Frankfurt, presumably for transmittal to the United States Delegation at
                    Babelsberg.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d801-f2" n="2" xml:id="d801-f2-content">
